"""One entry per sub-network: name, what it does, why it exists, grouped by family."""
F=[
('Getting events in','The browser reports raw facts, such as a key name or a button mask. Deciding what those facts mean is application logic, so it has to happen in neurons.',[
('bank and port wiring','Holds the shared wires that drive the memory, image and event ports, including the input neurons the glue writes into.','Ports are the only way out of the network. Several sub-networks use each port, so one place sums their addresses and enables. That avoids a duplicate port per feature.'),
('raw event interpretation','Turns key name code units, button masks, pointer types, field text and touch positions into cooked events. It also tells the browser whether its default action stands.','The glue is forbidden from knowing what Enter or a right click is. This network is what makes that rule possible.'),
('event dispatch','One neuron left from the first dispatcher. It did not fire on the key presses we traced.','Routing now lives in `raw event interpretation` and the state rules. It is listed so that the record stays complete.'),
('extended characters','Writes and reads UTF-8 for characters past Latin-1, joining and splitting surrogate pairs.','Cells keep browser code units, so paste and copy stay one to one. Only the file format needs bytes.'),
('character maps','Converts between Unicode and the internal character codes, using the Windows-1252 block.','Keeping internal codes small keeps glyph, metric and spelling tables small. Files and the clipboard still need Unicode.'),
('key handling','Maps each key and modifier combination to an editing command.','Shortcuts are behavior, so they live in weights instead of a key table in the glue.'),
('ribbon actions','Maps a clicked button id to its command.','The ribbon has many targets. One map lets the pointer path stay the same for all of them.'),
('screenshot hit test','Reads the object id under the pointer from the last screen. For text, it then uses the line table in memory to find the document position.','The screen already knows which object was drawn where, so buttons and menus need no separate table of rectangles.'),
('rv a3 interaction','Handles word and page motion, right click, autoscroll while dragging and the context menu. It also holds the later tier 1 features from `gen/t1_features.py`.','These editing motions need more than a single key rule, because they scan text and follow the pointer over many ticks.'),
('compiled control','Holds every state rule, compiled together: the gated sums that give each register its next value, plus the return dispatchers.','This is where features actually meet. A register written by many features has one sum here, with one gated term per rule that writes it.'),
('shared control registers','Holds editor state such as caret, selection and typing format, plus the comparators that order a selection.','Many features read the same state. Shared registers mean each feature does not keep its own copy that could fall out of step.'),
]),
('Changing the document','These networks are the only ones that write document text. They all go through the same edit and undo paths, so everything stays undoable.',[
('prompt bar','One bar that takes a short text and hands it to the command that asked: a color, a new style name, a new name for a style, or a font name.','These commands each need one line of text. One bar with one buffer does all of them, so no command has its own field.'),
('style create and rename','Writes a new style table entry from the format at the caret, renames a style with undo records, and applies a character style over a run.','Files and users both name styles. Keeping these in the style table means save, open and apply work for them with no new paths.'),
('list formats','Gives the list format menu, and reads numFmt and lvlText per level from a file.','A list format is a small number kept in the paragraph record. Splits, undo and clipboard then carry it with no extra work.'),
('view: side scroll and vertical ruler','Slides a page wider than the window, draws the bar along the foot, moves the slide to follow the caret, and draws the vertical ruler.','Above 150 percent a page no longer fits the window. The zoom map stays linear, with one more shift, so hit tests and paint still agree.'),
('view: wheel and thumb drag','Turns Shift+wheel and a sideways wheel delta into a slide of a wide page, and lets the thumb of the bar at the foot be dragged, at the scale that draws it.','The glue only reports raw deltas and modifier bits. Deciding that Shift means sideways, and mapping pointer travel to page travel, is application logic, so it lives in neurons that feed the existing slide path.'),
('zip crc check','After the dry inflate of the main part, runs its bytes through the save CRC network and compares with the CRC in the central directory; a mismatch refuses the file and keeps the document.','A corruption that still inflates to the stated size would otherwise open with wrong text. The CRC network already exists for save, so the check costs only three states and two registers.'),
('repeat last command','Remembers which kind of formatting command ran last; F4 enters that command again, whose registers still hold the last values.','Word users repeat a format onto the next selection with F4. The commands already keep their arguments in registers, so repeat needs only a kind register and one dispatch state.'),
('recent colors','Keeps the last eight exact text colors, newest first and without repeats, draws them in a row of the text color menu, and sends a clicked one back through the More Colors path.','A color picked from the grid or typed as hex is hard to find again. The list reuses the exact color path, so undo, save and the nearest palette entry come with it.'),
('column breaks','Ctrl+Shift+Enter splits the paragraph and marks the new one with a column break, with undo; reads and writes the break as w:br of type column.','A column break is the page break flag with a second value, so layout, undo and save reuse the page break paths. Layout only needs one more rule: in the first of two columns the paragraph moves to the second.'),
('vertical ruler drag','A press near the top or bottom margin edge on the vertical ruler starts a drag; the release sets that margin of the caret section, snapped to a sixteenth of an inch, unzoomed, with undo.','The vertical ruler only showed margins. Dragging them reuses the horizontal ruler release path and the section edit, so undo and relayout come with it.'),
('find across paragraphs','One matcher for queries that hold paragraph marks, shared by the replace walker, the match counter and the highlight.','A match that crosses a paragraph cannot be found inside one slot, so it needs state that follows the text across slots.'),
('find codes','Reads the Word find codes ^t ^l ^^ ^s ^- ^? ^# ^$ in the query and the character codes in the replacement, for the shared matcher, the walker, the counter and the highlight.','A code is two cells of the query that stand for one cell of the document, so the matcher needs to know them apart from plain text.'),
('tier 1 ribbon commands','Routes the Column Break, Text Wrapping and Comment ribbon commands to the column break, line break and comment paths.','A ribbon command passes no arguments, so a state sets them before the shared path runs.'),
('clipboard html','Writes an HTML twin of each copy (paragraphs, alignment, bold, italic, underline, size, color, font) and reads HTML pasted from other programs into runs and paragraphs.','Formatting crosses the system clipboard only as HTML, so the network writes and reads it, as it does the .docx XML.'),
('clipboard formatting','Keeps the style cells and paragraph records of the copy, and restores them when the pasted text equals that copy.','The system clipboard carries only text here. So the network keeps formatting in its own memory, and uses it when the pasted text matches.'),
('edit primitives','Inserts and deletes characters and paragraphs, and logs each change for undo.','It is the single choke point for edits, so undo cannot be bypassed by accident.'),
('undo','Walks the log backward and forward to undo and redo.','The log format is shared, so any feature that logs correctly gets undo with no extra network.'),
('range walker','Walks a selection for copy, cut, delete and formatting.','Selections cross paragraphs and slots. One walker holds that hard logic, and each command just supplies the action.'),
('bulk edits','Processes windows of many cells per tick for large formatting, copy, save, paste and find operations.','Going one cell per tick is too slow on a 100 page document. These walkers keep large operations usable.'),
('paste','Inserts clipboard text and splits it into paragraphs.','Pasted text arrives as a flat vector of code units, and the document stores paragraphs.'),
('find and replace','Runs a search automaton over the document, counts matches and replaces them.','Search needs its own scanning state, which is separate from the caret.'),
('tier 2','Implements style commands, paragraph commands, lists and typed font sizes.','These commands share paragraph records and a style table, so they are grouped around that data.'),
('a4 commands','Implements repeat, format painter and keep rules, among others.','These are small commands that reuse existing registers, and each needs only a few rules.'),
('a4 tabs','Handles tab stops.','A tab has no fixed width. Its advance depends on the current position, so layout needs a dedicated rule.'),
('tier3','Holds the remaining tier 3 commands, plus undo for their operations.','It connects tier 3 features to the shared undo log.'),
('tier 4 features','Implements tracked changes, fields, equations and mail merge.','These change what a run of text means, rather than how it looks.'),
('spell dictionary','Walks a word automaton held as a read only table, with one read per painted letter, and marks misspelled words.','An automaton checks a word at one step per letter. The table is built from the word list by merging identical subtrees, with no fitting.'),
('feat1 run effects','Decodes the extended field of a style entry for the glyph network: caps and small caps draw the capital, small capitals take a smaller size, hidden text takes no width or ink, and character spacing joins the advance.','These properties change what is drawn and how wide it is, so the glyph network must see them. One neuron answers for the usual character that has none of them.'),
('feat1 docx reader','Reads caps, small caps, double strike, hidden text, character spacing, run shading, links and their targets, bookmarks, contextual spacing and widow control.','Each lands in a field of the interned style entry or a paragraph cell, so edits, undo and the clipboard carry it with no new path.'),
('feat1 docx writer','Writes those properties back, opens and closes links and bookmarks around runs, and lists external link targets as relationships.','A file that is opened and saved should keep what it had, even where the editor has no command for it yet.'),
('feat2 built up math','Builds, measures, paints, saves and prints the newer equation forms: a root with an index, sums, products and integrals with limits, five accents, delimiters as tall as their line, and a two row matrix. Reads them back from OMML as their linear form.','Each form is one character standing for a record, as fractions and roots already were, so editing, undo and layout carry them with no new path. A delimiter is its own record, so what stands between two of them can itself be built up.'),
('feat2 pdf run effects','Prints character spacing as text spacing, run shading under the text, double strike as two lines, and external links as link annotations of the page.','These properties already live in the style entry and on screen; a printed page should show what the screen shows, and a link should still work.'),
('style interner','Finds or adds a style record in the interned table, in its own clock domain.','Each character stores a short index instead of a full record. That makes the text compact and makes comparing two styles a single check.'),
]),
('Laying out and painting the page','These networks decide where everything goes, then draw it.',[
('line breaking','Finds where lines break, and handles alignment.','Every paragraph needs it, and it runs on each edit, so it has to be small.'),
('zoom','Handles zoom levels from 50 to 150 percent and read mode, maps paint to the screen at the chosen scale, and runs the status bar controls.','Paint works in page coordinates. This keeps the many drawing paths unaware of the zoom level.'),
('layout and paint','Walks paragraphs and places lines and words. It draws text, selection and pictures.','It is the main drawing loop. Most features add to this one walk, so they do not repaint separately.'),
('chrome','Draws the caret, scrollbar and status bar, and handles autoscroll.','These change on most events and must update without repainting the page.'),
('ribbon display list','One sequencer that plays draw records for the ribbon, menus and labels from read only memory, one item per tick.','Drawing a ribbon is data more than logic. Its neurons are shared by every list, and the lists themselves cost no neurons.'),
('canvas look','Draws the page shadow and the canvas around the page.','This is the appearance around the page, kept separate because it does not depend on the document.'),
('pointer','Draws the mouse pointer, saves and restores the colors under it, and chooses its shape from the screen.','The output is one image, with no system cursor over it. So the network has to draw the pointer and clean up after it.'),
('screen check','Compares one line of the id plane with the line table on each blink tick, and repairs it by repainting.','The project requires checking the screen against document state. This catches drawing damage as the app runs.'),
('a4 ruler','Draws the ruler and handles dragging its markers.','The ruler both displays and edits paragraph properties, so it needs its own drawing and pointer logic.'),
('a4 keep','Applies keep with next and keep lines during pagination.','It has to add up the height a paragraph must share a page with before placing its first line.'),
('a4 borders','Draws paragraph borders and shading, on screen and in PDF.','Neighboring paragraphs can join borders, so this cannot be drawn one paragraph at a time.'),
('a4 pagenum','Handles page number formats and section start values.','Page numbers depend on sections, and they have to come out the same on screen and in a PDF.'),
('tables','Scans tables, inserts them, edits rows and columns, applies shading, and handles border hit zones and dragging.','A table has structure that must stay consistent as rows and columns change, and borders are also click targets.'),
('a4 merge','Handles merged table cells.','Merging breaks the simple grid that the table walker assumes, so it needs its own rules.'),
('sections','Holds section records, section breaks and page setup.','Page size, margins and columns can change partway through a document.'),
('pictures','Draws picture handles, resizes pictures by resampling, writes PNG and reads pictures from a file.','A picture is the one document object that is not text, so it has its own storage and drawing path.'),
('notes and balloons','Draws wrapped text, comment balloons and footnotes.','These flow outside the normal text column, and they take space from the page or margin.'),
('headers and footers','Holds header and footer strings and their edit bar.','They repeat on each page, and they are edited separately from the main text.'),
('table of contents','Builds and updates the table of contents.','It has to scan headings and their final page numbers, which are known only after layout.'),
]),
('Drawing text','This is the largest family. It is what replaces a font engine. The method is described in [How a letter gets drawn](#how-a-letter-gets-drawn).',[
('glyph weights (outline edges)','Holds the font outlines as edge neurons, one small program per glyph.','This is the font itself, written as weights. It accounts for most of the neurons, since eight families with their faces hold many edges.'),
('glyph unit','Runs the drawing of one glyph, in its own clock domain.','Paint can stall while a glyph is generated, and that keeps the paint loop simple.'),
('glyph network','Selects and addresses a character cell for drawing.','It is the junction between layout and drawing, whichever way the glyph is produced.'),
('glyph metrics','Holds advance widths and kerning as decision trees.','Layout needs widths for each character, and it should not have to draw a glyph to learn one.'),
('ramp bank','Provides shared ramps, `R_q = relu(q - x)`, that turn a crossing into pixel shares.','Ramps are the same for all glyphs, so one bank serves every edge. Each glyph does not need its own.'),
('coverage','Adds edge shares into pixel coverage, and once per row adds the share of whole blocks of columns from one delta per crossing.','It turns signed crossings into how much of a pixel is ink, which gives smooth edges.'),
('snapping layer','Fits outline heights to the pixel grid for a given size.','Unsnapped text looks blurry at small sizes, so heights move to whole pixels using font metrics. Horizontal snapping is written, but no font uses it now, because it looked worse side by side.'),
('glyph geometry','Scales outline coordinates by the drawn size.','A single set of weights can then serve any size, rather than storing outlines per size.'),
('row sequencer','Steps the glyph unit through the rows of a character.','Coverage builds one sample line per tick, so something has to count them.'),
('glyph pixel records','Records a small glyph drawn black on white, so that later draws take one read and one patch.','Most repaint cost was glyph rows. Replaying a record is much cheaper for the common case of plain text.'),
('glyph store','Keeps drawn glyphs in memory and copies them to the screen.','Generating a glyph costs far more than copying one, and most letters repeat.'),
('glyph patch','Assembles coverage and color into a patch for the patch port.','Text color is applied here, so a cached glyph works in any color.'),
('stem units','Would hold stem positions for horizontal snapping. It has no neurons in the current build, because no font turns that on.','It is listed so that the provenance record stays complete.'),
]),
('Reading files','Each of these exists because no parser library is allowed. XML, zip and PNG bytes are consumed one state at a time.',[
('docx reader','Unzips the file, inflates it and parses the document XML.','It is the core of opening a file. The goal requires that networks do parsing and decompression.'),
('docx reader tier 2','Reads styles, numbering, and run and paragraph properties.','Formatting in `.docx` is scattered across several parts and elements.'),
('docx reader tier 3','Adds walking between the parts of a file.','Tier 3 content lives in separate parts of the zip file.'),
('docx reader notes','Reads footnote, comment and header parts.','Each of these has its own XML part that must be connected back to the main text.'),
('docx reader tier 4','Reads tracked marks and fields.','These wrap ordinary runs in extra elements, so they add state to the parser.'),
('docx reader rv_a5','Improves fidelity on files from other programs: nested tables, row spans, spacing and truncated content. It also holds spell suggestions and the saved list of added words.','Real files use forms that a simple reader misses. The spelling parts sit here only because of where they were added in the generator.'),
('a4 docx','Reads and writes the paragraph properties added by the commands above.','Anything the app can do must survive a save and open, so features carry their own file code.'),
('png reader','Decodes PNG files to pixel words, with limits on bad input.','Pictures in a `.docx` are usually PNG, and they have to become pixels the network can draw.'),
]),
('Writing files','Saving runs the same idea in reverse. The network produces every byte, and the glue only offers the download.',[
('docx writer','Writes the document XML parts.','A saved file needs XML text with the values of this document filled in.'),
('docx writer tier 3','Writes section properties, tabs, markers, comments, notes, headers and footers.','These features add elements and whole parts to the saved file.'),
('docx deflate','Compresses with LZ77 and fixed Huffman codes.','`.docx` files are compressed zip files, and compression has to happen in the network too.'),
('docx crc','Computes CRC32 of the bytes written to the zip file.','Zip readers reject a file with a wrong checksum. It holds four 256 entry tables as weights, so it can process four bytes at once.'),
('zip container','Keeps the member table, and writes the central directory and table XML.','The directory at the end of a zip file has to list the size and offset of each part.'),
('pdf writer','Writes PDF objects, text and pictures.','Print to PDF is in the goal, and PDF has its own structure of objects and offsets.'),
('pdf tables','Writes PDF page size, table rules and shading.','Table lines are drawn as PDF commands, not as characters.'),
('file output command','Selects the length, data start and file name that the glue saves.','The glue must not decide what to save, or under what name. It reads these neurons and acts.'),
]),
]
